## 10. Error Analysis

### 10.1 Failure Taxonomy

| Failure Type | Description | Frequency | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| `same_chapter_confusion` | Correct chapter retrieved, wrong verse | ~40–50% of failures | Query "action vs inaction" → BG_3_3 instead of BG_3_8 |
| `theme_confusion` | Verse with partial theme overlap retrieved | ~35–45% of failures | Query "mind as enemy" → BG_12_8 (mind+devotion) instead of BG_6_6 |
| `wrong_retrieval` | No meaningful overlap | ~10–15% of failures | Short ambiguous keyword queries |

### 10.2 Query Difficulty Distribution

```
Easiest queries (Recall@1 ≈ 1.0):
  • Transliteration queries (direct text match signal)
  • Long descriptive queries with rare keywords
  • Queries containing unique verse-specific terms

Hardest queries (Recall@1 ≈ 0.0):
  • Short 1-2 word keyword queries ("eternal", "liberation")
  • Queries where multiple verses are equally valid answers
  • Queries using thematic synonyms not in training data
```

### 10.3 Cross-Lingual Performance

| Query Language | Expected Recall@1 | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| English (template) | Highest | Directly trained on these |
| English (paraphrase) | High | Model generalises well |
| Transliteration | High | Sub-word overlap with document |
| Hindi | Medium | Cross-lingual transfer |
| Sanskrit Devanagari | Medium | Strong for exact phrases |

