```

---

## Quick-Start Reference

```python
# 1. Load the fine-tuned model
from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer
model = SentenceTransformer("./sanskrit-retrieval-model-mnrl")

# 2. Initialise RAG system
rag = SanskritRAGSystem(model=model, corpus=raw_corpus, top_k=3)

# 3. Query in any supported language
print(rag.query("What does the Gita say about karma?"))
print(rag.query("yada yada hi dharmasya"))
print(rag.query("How to control the restless mind?"))
print(rag.query("कर्म का सिद्धांत क्या है?"))

# 4. Direct retrieval (no formatting)
results = rag.retrieve("soul is eternal")
for verse in results:
    print(verse["id"], verse["retrieval_score"], verse["translation"][:80])
```

